From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:08:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Preserve resolved shell init on config read failures

Cache every successful shell-init policy read and warn once per exception type/message when falling back. Keep first-read defaults explicit rather than silently substituting startup semantics.

Proof: parent b12b7ea426e7: 2 passed / 8 failed; fixed: 35 passed across shell-init, login PATH and isolated HTTP readback suites. Real localhost 503 reproduction covers snapshot and login fallback. Four condition mutants killed.
---
